      {
        "body": "In 2 of 5 live drive runs (1 and 3), releasing the hold chord through Hyprland's generated Lua release binding did not end the take: job_dict_1 duration_ms=11000 (the fixture's end) instead of ~2600, and the double tap's tap release had no effect. The drive's hold step still passed because it waits 60 s for idle. A separate 5x uinput rig through the same binding shape delivered every release (s7-release-rig.log), so the cause (Hyprland not running the release command, or the daemon answering none) is unconfirmed; no-op edges are not logged at info. Evidence: qa-evidence/run-1793539833-3764215 and run-1793540078-3780158 daemon.log; memory .flow/memory/bug/integration/hyprland-hold-release-sometimes-never-2026-11-01.md (surface: crates/dettivo-qa/src/scenarios/hotkeys_hyprland.rs)",
